Package: future.p2p
Title: Parallel Future Backend for Peer-to-Peer Clusters using 'pico.sh'
Version: 0.6.0-9007
Description: Implementation of the Future API <doi:10.32614/RJ-2021-048>
    that resolves futures on a peer-to-peer ('P2P') cluster, where you and
    your friends share your spare compute resources with each other. The
    backend is fully compliant with the Future API, as validated by the
    'future.tests' conformance test suite, meaning that code using futures
    gives identical results and behaves the same regardless of which future
    backend is used. A common use is to parallelize existing map-reduce
    calls via the 'futurize' package <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2601.17578>, e.g.
    'plan(future.p2p::cluster)' followed by 'lapply(xs, fcn) |> futurize()'
    or 'purrr::map(xs, fcn) |> futurize()'.
Imports:
    future (>= 1.80.0),
    processx,
    callr,
    utils
Suggests:
    commonmark,
    base64enc
